  "id": "COMPOUND:24715 - PROTEIN:4886",
  "verbalization": "Galphin A is implicated in the activation of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR through a multi-step pathway involving Alpha-actinin-1 and other compounds. The evidence suggests that Galphin A directly targets Alpha-actinin-1, which in turn is a target of Eucommiol or (4R)-Dihydro-4-hydroxy-3-methylene-2(3H)-furanone, both of which ultimately interact with ATR. This indicates that Galphin A's effects are mediated through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately converge on ATR. The presence of multiple pathways converging on ATR supports the idea that Galphin A may influence ATR through different molecular intermediates, potentially through distinct mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the signaling network and underscores the role of Galphin A in modulating ATR activity, which could have implications for therapeutic strategies targeting this kinase.",
